{"id":"mahabharata-3-029","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":29,"title":"एकोनत्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 29 · Prahlada's counsel on forgiveness and might","summary":{"en":"Draupadi recounts the old dialogue in which Prahlada taught his grandson Bali that neither constant forgiveness nor constant fierceness is right: the wise king knows when to forgive and when to show his might. Now, she says, is the time for might.","kn":"ಸದಾ ಕ್ಷಮೆಯೂ ಸದಾ ಕಠೋರತೆಯೂ ಸರಿಯಲ್ಲ, ಯಾವಾಗ ಕ್ಷಮಿಸಬೇಕು ಯಾವಾಗ ಬಲ ತೋರಬೇಕು ಎಂದು ಜ್ಞಾನಿ ರಾಜನು ಅರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ ಎಂದು ಪ್ರಹ್ಲಾದನು ಮೊಮ್ಮಗ ಬಲಿಗೆ ಉಪದೇಶಿಸಿದ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ಸಂವಾದವನ್ನು ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಈಗ ಬಲ ತೋರುವ ಸಮಯ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"द्रौपदी वह प्राचीन संवाद सुनाती हैं जिसमें प्रह्लाद ने अपने पौत्र बलि को सिखाया कि न सदा क्षमा उचित है, न सदा कठोरता: बुद्धिमान राजा जानता है कि कब क्षमा करे और कब बल दिखाए। वे कहती हैं कि अब बल का समय है।","te":"ఎప్పుడూ క్షమ, ఎప్పుడూ కాఠిన్యం సరికాదని, ఎప్పుడు క్షమించాలో ఎప్పుడు బలం చూపాలో జ్ఞానియైన రాజుకు తెలుసని ప్రహ్లాదుడు తన మనవడు బలికి ఉపదేశించిన ప్రాచీన సంవాదాన్ని ద్రౌపది చెబుతుంది. ఇప్పుడు బలం చూపే సమయమంటుంది.","ta":"எப்போதும் மன்னிப்பதும் சரியல்ல, எப்போதும் கடுமையாக இருப்பதும் சரியல்ல, எப்போது மன்னிக்க வேண்டும் எப்போது வலிமை காட்ட வேண்டும் என்று ஞானமுள்ள மன்னன் அறிவான் என்று ப்ரஹ்லாதன் பேரன் பலிக்குப் போதித்த பழைய உரையாடலைத் திரௌபதி சொல்கிறாள். இப்போது வலிமை காட்டும் நேரம் என்கிறாள்.","ml":"പ്രഹ്ലാദൻ തന്റെ പേരക്കുട്ടിയായ ബലിയെ പഠിപ്പിച്ച പഴയ സംഭാഷണം ദ്രൗപദി ഓർമ്മിക്കുന്നു: നിരന്തരമായ ക്ഷമയും നിരന്തരമായ ക്രൂരതയും ശരിയല്ല; ബുദ്ധിമാനായ രാജാവ് ക്ഷമിക്കേണ്ട സമയവും ശക്തി കാണിക്കേണ്ട സമയവും അറിയുന്നു. ഇപ്പോൾ ശക്തി കാണിക്കേണ്ട സമയമാണെന്ന് അവൾ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.29; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nप्रह्लादस्य च संवादं बलेर्वैरोचनस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On this very point they recount an ancient tale, the conversation between Prahlada and Bali, son of Virochana."}},{"n":2,"text":"असुरेन्द्रं महाप्राज्ञं धर्माणामागतागमम् ।\nबलिः पप्रच्छ दैत्येन्द्रं प्रह्लादं पितरं पितुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bali questioned Prahlada, lord of the Daityas and of the asuras, greatly wise and learned in the traditions of dharma, his own father's father."}},{"n":3,"text":"क्षमा स्विच्छ्रेयसी तात उताहो तेज इत्युत ।\nएतन्मे संशयं तात यथावद्ब्रूहि पृच्छते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Grandfather, which is better, forgiveness or fierce might? Please tell me truly, as I ask, this doubt of mine.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"श्रेयो यदत्र धर्मज्ञ ब्रूहि मे तदसंशयम् ।\nकरिष्यामि हि तत्सर्वं यथावदनुशासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Knower of dharma, tell me without doubt what is best in this matter; I will carry out all your instruction exactly.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"तस्मै प्रोवाच तत्सर्वमेवं पृष्टः पितामहः ।\nसर्वनिश्चयवित्प्राज्ञः संशयं परिपृच्छते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Asked so, his grandfather, wise and knowing the conclusion on every matter, told him all as the questioner sought to resolve his doubt."}},{"text":"प्रह्लाद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Prahlada said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"न श्रेयः सततं तेजो न नित्यं श्रेयसी क्षमा ।\nइति तात विजानीहि द्वयमेतदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Neither might is always best nor is forgiveness always best; know, my child, without doubt that both are true.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"यो नित्यं क्षमते तात बहून्दोषान्स विन्दति ।\nभृत्याः परिभवन्त्येनमुदासीनास्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man who always forgives, my child, meets many troubles: servants and neutral people alike despise him.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"सर्वभूतानि चाप्यस्य न नमन्ते कदाचन ।\nतस्मान्नित्यं क्षमा तात पण्डितैरपवादिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"No creature ever bows to him, and so the wise have condemned constant forgiveness.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"अवज्ञाय हि तं भृत्या भजन्ते बहुदोषताम् ।\nआदातुं चास्य वित्तानि प्रार्थयन्तेऽल्पचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Servants who disregard him fall into many faults, and the small-minded long to take his wealth.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"यानं वस्त्राण्यलंकाराञ्शयनान्यासनानि च ।\nभोजनान्यथ पानानि सर्वोपकरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Carriages, clothes, ornaments, beds, seats, food, drink and every kind of furnishing:\""}},{"n":11,"text":"आददीरन्नधिकृता यथाकाममचेतसः ।\nप्रदिष्टानि च देयानि न दद्युर्भर्तृशासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"those in authority, being senseless, take them at will, and they do not give what they are ordered to give, in spite of their master's command.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"न चैनं भर्तृपूजाभिः पूजयन्ति कदाचन ।\nअवज्ञानं हि लोकेऽस्मिन्मरणादपि गर्हितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They never honor him with the honor due a master; and in this world contempt is worse than death.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"क्षमिणं तादृशं तात ब्रुवन्ति कटुकान्यपि ।\nप्रेष्याः पुत्राश्च भृत्याश्च तथोदासीनवृत्तयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Slaves, sons, servants and even neutral people say harsh things, my child, to such a forgiving man.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"अप्यस्य दारानिच्छन्ति परिभूय क्षमावतः ।\nदाराश्चास्य प्रवर्तन्ते यथाकाममचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Disdaining the forgiving man, they even desire his wives, and his wives behave senselessly as they please.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"तथा च नित्यमुदिता यदि स्वल्पमपीश्वरात् ।\nदण्डमर्हन्ति दुष्यन्ति दुष्टाश्चाप्यपकुर्वते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And ever pleased, even the slightest punishment they deserve from their master they take as a fault, and the wicked do harm.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"एते चान्ये च बहवो नित्यं दोषाः क्षमावताम् ।\nअथ वैरोचने दोषानिमान्विद्ध्यक्षमावताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These and many other faults always befall the forgiving. Now hear, son of Virochana, the faults of those who do not forgive.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अस्थाने यदि वा स्थाने सततं रजसावृतः ।\nक्रुद्धो दण्डान्प्रणयति विविधान्स्वेन तेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man ever covered with passion, in the wrong place or in the right, angrily metes out varied punishments by his own force.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"मित्रैः सह विरोधं च प्राप्नुते तेजसावृतः ।\nप्राप्नोति द्वेष्यतां चैव लोकात्स्वजनतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Overcome by his fierceness, he comes into quarrel with friends and becomes hated by the world and by his own people.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"सोऽवमानादर्थहानिमुपालम्भमनादरम् ।\nसंतापद्वेषलोभांश्च शत्रूंश्च लभते नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From contempt, such a man suffers loss of wealth, blame and disrespect, and gains torment, hatred, greed and enemies.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"क्रोधाद्दण्डान्मनुष्येषु विविधान्पुरुषो नयन् ।\nभ्रश्यते शीघ्रमैश्वर्यात्प्राणेभ्यः स्वजनादपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man who angrily inflicts various punishments on people soon falls from his rule, his life, and his kin.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"योऽपकर्तॄंश्च कर्तॄंश्च तेजसैवोपगच्छति ।\nतस्मादुद्विजते लोकः सर्पाद्वेश्मगतादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who deals with both wrongdoers and benefactors only through fierce force, the world fears as a snake in the house.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"यस्मादुद्विजते लोकः कथं तस्य भवो भवेत् ।\nअन्तरं ह्यस्य दृष्ट्वैव लोको विकुरुते ध्रुवम् ।\nतस्मान्नात्युत्सृजेत्तेजो न च नित्यं मृदुर्भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How can one whom the world fears prosper? People see his weak point and turn against him for certain. So one should neither use all one's force nor always be gentle.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"काले मृदुर्यो भवति काले भवति दारुणः ।\nस वै सुखमवाप्नोति लोकेऽमुष्मिन्निहैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He who is gentle at the right time and harsh at the right time gains happiness both in this world and the next.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"क्षमाकालांस्तु वक्ष्यामि शृणु मे विस्तरेण तान् ।\nये ते नित्यमसंत्याज्या यथा प्राहुर्मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Now I will tell you the times for forgiveness; hear them in detail, those which the wise say should never be abandoned.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"पूर्वोपकारी यस्तु स्यादपराधेऽगरीयसि ।\nउपकारेण तत्तस्य क्षन्तव्यमपराधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If a man who has done you a favor before commits some small offense, that offender should be forgiven in return for his favor.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"अबुद्धिमाश्रितानां च क्षन्तव्यमपराधिनाम् ।\nन हि सर्वत्र पाण्डित्यं सुलभं पुरुषेण वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those who offend through ignorance should also be forgiven, for wisdom is not easy for a man to have everywhere.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"अथ चेद्बुद्धिजं कृत्वा ब्रूयुस्ते तदबुद्धिजम् ।\nपापान्स्वल्पेऽपि तान्हन्यादपराधे तथानृजून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But if they do wrong deliberately and then claim it was unintentional, one should kill those wicked and crooked men even for a slight offense.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"सर्वस्यैकोऽपराधस्ते क्षन्तव्यः प्राणिनो भवेत् ।\nद्वितीये सति वध्यस्तु स्वल्पेऽप्यपकृते भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Every creature's first offense should be forgiven; with a second, he deserves to be punished even for a small wrong.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"अजानता भवेत्कश्चिदपराधः कृतो यदि ।\nक्षन्तव्यमेव तस्याहुः सुपरीक्ष्य परीक्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If someone has committed an offense unknowingly, they say he should be forgiven, after careful examination.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"मृदुना मार्दवं हन्ति मृदुना हन्ति दारुणम् ।\nनासाध्यं मृदुना किंचित्तस्मात्तीक्ष्णतरो मृदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The gentle man overcomes gentleness and the gentle man overcomes harshness; nothing is impossible for the gentle, so the gentle man is sharper than the sharp.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"देशकालौ तु संप्रेक्ष्य बलाबलमथात्मनः ।\nनादेशकाले किंचित्स्याद्देशः कालः प्रतीक्ष्यते ।\nतथा लोकभयाच्चैव क्षन्तव्यमपराधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Considering place and time and one's own strength or weakness, one acts; nothing should be done at the wrong place or time, so one waits for the right place and time. And also out of fear of public opinion, offenders should be forgiven.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"एत एवंविधाः कालाः क्षमायाः परिकीर्तिताः ।\nअतोऽन्यथानुवर्तत्सु तेजसः काल उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These are the occasions declared for forgiveness; in cases other than these, it is said, the time for might has come.\""}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"तदहं तेजसः कालं तव मन्ये नराधिप ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रेषु लुब्धेषु सततं चापकारिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So, O lord of men, I think this is the time for might for you, against the greedy sons of Dhritarashtra, who always do wrong.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"न हि कश्चित्क्षमाकालो विद्यतेऽद्य कुरून्प्रति ।\nतेजसश्चागते काले तेज उत्स्रष्टुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is now no time for forgiveness toward the Kurus at all; when the time for might has come, you should unleash your might.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"मृदुर्भवत्यवज्ञातस्तीक्ष्णादुद्विजते जनः ।\nकाले प्राप्ते द्वयं ह्येतद्यो वेद स महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The scorned man grows gentle, and people dread the fierce one; the king who knows both and acts when the time comes is a true protector of the earth.\""}}]}]}